{"builder":"Goal: add a new tool, jsonl-lint, as the first npm workspace under packages/ in suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test, all in one pull request that closes issue https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102.\n\nContext: right now packages/ does not exist. The root package.json has workspaces [\"packages/*\"], and its test script runs `npm test --workspaces --if-present`. The CI workflow .github/workflows/test.yml runs `npm ci` and then `npm test` on Node 22. Tools are plain ES modules on Node 22+, with no build step and no runtime dependencies. Tests use node:test.\n\nSteps:\n1. Create packages/jsonl-lint/package.json with: \"name\": \"jsonl-lint\", \"type\": \"module\", \"scripts\": { \"test\": \"node --test\" }, and a \"bin\" entry { \"jsonl-lint\": \"bin/jsonl-lint.js\" }. Do not add a \"dependencies\" field (or leave it empty). Mark it private if you like and set engines node >=22.\n2. Create packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js and export `lint(text)`. It takes the file's text and returns an array of `{ line, error }`, one entry for each row that is not valid JSON:\n   - Split on \"\\n\" and also strip a trailing \"\\r\" so CRLF files work. Line numbers are 1-based and count every physical line, including blank ones.\n   - Skip blank lines (empty, or only whitespace).\n   - A last line with no newline after it (an unterminated or torn last row) still gets checked with JSON.parse like every other line. The empty string after a final newline is not a row.\n   - `error` is the JSON.parse error message string.\n   - Valid text, empty text, or text with only blank lines returns [].\n3. Create packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js, executable (chmod +x, with the `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang). It imports lint from ../src/index.js. Behaviour:\n   - No argument: print a usage message to stderr and exit 2.\n   - The file is missing or cannot be read: print an error naming the file to stderr and exit 2.\n   - Otherwise, for each problem print `<file>:<line>: <error>` to stdout, where <file> is the argument exactly as the user gave it. Exit 1 if there were any problems and 0 if there were none.\n   - Set process.exitCode instead of calling process.exit straight after writing, so the output is not cut off.\n4. Add node:test tests under packages/jsonl-lint/test/ (for example test/lint.test.js and test/cli.test.js) so that `node --test` finds them when run from packages/jsonl-lint. Cover each of these with its own test:\n   - a clean file → [] / exit 0, nothing on stdout;\n   - a bad middle row → reported with the correct 1-based line;\n   - a torn last row (invalid JSON with no trailing newline) → reported;\n   - blank lines → skipped, and they still count toward the line numbers of later rows;\n   - the exit codes: run the bin with child_process (spawnSync of process.execPath) and check for 0 on a clean file, 1 on a bad file (with stdout matching `<file>:<line>: `), 2 with no argument, and 2 on a missing file (with stderr not empty).\n   Write fixtures to a temp dir (fs.mkdtempSync of os.tmpdir()) or keep them under test/fixtures.\n5. Create packages/jsonl-lint/README.md that explains what the tool does, its usage, the output format, the exit codes (0/1/2) and the lint(text) API.\n6. Update the root README.md: replace the \"No tools yet: `packages/` is empty...\" bullet with a bullet that lists packages/jsonl-lint (jsonl-lint) and a short description.\n7. Run `npm install` at the root so package-lock.json picks up the new workspace. Commit the updated package-lock.json, because CI runs `npm ci`, and that fails if the lock is out of sync. Then run `npm ci && npm test` at the root and make sure it passes, with the jsonl-lint tests actually running.\n8. Check by hand: `printf '{\"a\":1}\\n\\nnope\\n{\"b\":2}\\n{\"c\":' > /tmp/x.jsonl; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js /tmp/x.jsonl; echo $?` should print lines for 3 and 5 and exit 1. Also try no argument and a missing path, both of which should exit 2 with stderr output.\n9. Open exactly one pull request on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test. Its body must contain the line `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`. Wait until the `test` workflow check on the PR head is green; if it fails, fix it and push to the same PR.","verifier":"Check the pull request for issue https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102 with its head commit checked out. Run `npm ci` at the root first. There is one check per expect line, in order.\n\nCheck 1. Expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none\".\nRun:\n  d=$(mktemp -d)\n  printf '{\"a\":1}\\n\\nnope\\n  \\n{\"b\":2}\\n{\"c\":' > $d/bad.jsonl\n  node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $d/bad.jsonl; echo \"exit=$?\"\n  printf '{\"a\":1}\\n\\n[1,2]\\n\"s\"\\n' > $d/ok.jsonl\n  node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $d/ok.jsonl; echo \"exit=$?\"\n  printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":' > $d/torn.jsonl\n  node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $d/torn.jsonl; echo \"exit=$?\"\nPASS if all of these hold:\n  - For bad.jsonl, stdout has exactly two problem lines: one that starts with `$d/bad.jsonl:3: ` followed by a non-empty error, and one that starts with `$d/bad.jsonl:6: ` followed by a non-empty error. Nothing is reported for the blank lines 2 and 4 or the valid lines 1 and 5, and the exit status is 1.\n  - ok.jsonl prints no problem lines and exits 0.\n  - torn.jsonl reports `$d/torn.jsonl:2: <error>` and exits 1.\nFAIL if any problem line is missing, has the wrong line number, or has a different shape from `<file>:<line>: <error>`; if a blank or valid line is reported; if the unterminated last line is not reported; or if either exit status is wrong.\n\nCheck 2. Expect: \"A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2\".\nRun: `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js 2>err1; echo $?` and `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js /nonexistent/nope.jsonl 2>err2; echo $?`.\nPASS if both exit 2 and err1 and err2 are both non-empty. FAIL if either exits with something other than 2, or writes nothing to stderr.\n\nCheck 3. Expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]\".\nRun: `node --input-type=module -e \"import { lint } from './packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\nbad\\n'))); console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\n')));\"`\nPASS if the file exports a function named lint; the first call returns an array of one object with `line` equal to 2 and a truthy `error`; and the second call returns an empty array. FAIL if the import fails, lint is not exported, or the return value does not have the shape [{ line, error }].\n\nCheck 4. Expect: \"The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runtime dependencies, and node:test tests for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes\".\nRun: `node -e \"const p=require('./packages/jsonl-lint/package.json'); console.log(p.name, p.type, p.scripts&&p.scripts.test, JSON.stringify(p.dependencies||{}))\"`, then `(cd packages/jsonl-lint && npm test)`, then read the test files under packages/jsonl-lint.\nPASS if: name is `jsonl-lint`; type is `module`; scripts.test is `node --test` (extra flags after it are acceptable); dependencies is missing or empty; the tests import from `node:test` and pass when run; and among the tests there are cases for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn (unterminated) last row, blank lines, and the CLI exit codes. FAIL if any field is wrong, there is a runtime dependency, the tests fail, or any of the five cases has no test.\n\nCheck 5. Expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool\".\nRun: `test -f packages/jsonl-lint/README.md && echo yes` and `grep -n jsonl-lint README.md`.\nPASS if the package README exists and the root README.md mentions jsonl-lint in its list of tools. FAIL if either is missing.\n\nCheck 6. Expect: \"The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head\".\nRun: `gh pr view <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --json body,headRefOid,state` and `gh pr checks <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test`. Also run `npm ci && npm test` at the root at the head.\nPASS if the PR is on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test; its body contains `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`; it is the single PR for this change; local `npm test` exits 0; and the `test` workflow check at the head commit has passed. FAIL if the body lacks the Closes line, the work is split across PRs, npm test fails, or the test check is failing or missing at the head.\n\nAdvisory (not pass/fail):\n- Check that the error text after `<line>: ` is the JSON.parse message.\n- Check that CRLF files do not produce false errors.\n- Check that package-lock.json includes the new workspace, so that `npm ci` stays in sync.\n- Check that the bin is executable and has a node shebang."}